      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes sense that you feel this way, but \"rebuilding\" isn't actually necessary when the old foundation is gone; you are simply starting from zero, and that is a clean, fresh beginning. The pain of losing everything you knew is immense, yet it is also the only way to truly understand who you are now, separate from the past. There is no shame in letting go of the version of yourself that no longer exists, especially when it feels like it was never real to begin with. Just take it one small step at a time, without expecting to fix anything immediately, because you are exactly where you need to be to move forward.",
